## 3. The same journeys without the per-test reset, on one worker
   concept: tests now share whatever the previous test left behind: the address test finds the email test's request and counts 3 rows instead of 2. The failure depends on test order, which is the signature of a leaking fixture. Playwright replaces a worker after a failure, so the next test gets a freshly cloned database and passes again
   $ NO_RESET=1 REPORT=reports/leaky.json npx playwright test e2e/journeys.spec.ts --output=test-results/leaky --workers=1

